      "body": "# [NPU] Mask rotate-left input to 32 bits before widening shifts\n\nThe 32-bit Murmur rotation can receive a value whose high bits survive conversion to uint64 on the evaluated NPU Triton path. Those bits enter the right-shift term before the final output mask, producing incorrect hash values and therefore different deterministic sampling inputs. Mask the converted value with 0xFFFFFFFF before performing either shift. The hash constants, seed/position/column inputs and sampling configuration remain unchanged.\n\nThis is a shared sampling helper correction, not a model-specific answer patch. It applies to callers of rotl32; the runtime implementation is not guarded to NPU even though the recorded device regression is NPU. No other sampler or model code is included.\n\n## Base and exact source\n\nTarget release/v0.5.20, commit 94602c9c2b7cbdb8efd5c52802dac6a1c180089e. The upstream murmur_hash.py SHA-256 e932e4a7c5ae39eadc6400cc74ef4e646eaedc8370061e52b97a2544bbb5919b matches both the installed-package RECORD audit and saved original. The one-line patch applies strictly; the resulting SHA-256 da6fb278a230ed543a42981ca65b3322a46f3dc937c7b65f4475da9acffcea94 exactly matches the evaluated candidate. This draft targets the measured release, not an untested main forward port.\n\n## Preserved validation\n\n- Existing 8 seed/position rows x 16 columns = 128 vector outputs compared against the independent 32-bit reference: original 72 mismatches; corrected 0 mismatches.\n- [murmur_vector_results.json](https://github.com/celestial-micha/sglang/tree/9d08f82a76474a5693c3030df8c319d2d09c1e95/test/manual/murmur_uint32/murmur_vector_results.json) retains seeds, positions, expected/original/corrected outputs and counts. The counts were independently recomputed from this saved JSON during submission preparation; this was not a fresh device run.\n- [test_murmur_uint32_npu.py](https://github.com/celestial-micha/sglang/tree/9d08f82a76474a5693c3030df8c319d2d09c1e95/test/manual/murmur_uint32/test_murmur_uint32_npu.py) is the existing focused high-bit regression (16 columns). Run it with pytest on an Ascend NPU; it skips when NPU is absent. Its fixed expected values are a hash regression oracle, not hardcoded model responses.\n\nNo NPU experiment was rerun for this publication preparation. The vector proof establishes the integer hash correction on the measured stack; it does not claim GPU validation, every sampling configuration, or that remaining generated-audio/text differences are resolved. Later model-level quality work is outside this one-line PR.\n\n\n## Publication preparation checks\n\nAll included Python files parse successfully, with AST equivalence to the frozen measured/prepared source verified after comment/format-only submission cleanup. Available ruff F401/F821/UP037 checks pass. Required side-effect registration/initialization imports are retained with explicit noqa reasons. Newly added files/tests pass ruff formatting; existing large product files were not reformatted or reordered. Exact repository-pinned full pre-commit hooks were not run. No hardware experiment was rerun. The delivery manifest distinguishes frozen evidence SHA-256 values from submitted formatting-only file hashes.\n\n\n## Submission links\n\nEvaluated-source submission: https://github.com/celestial-micha/sglang/commit/9d08f82a76474a5693c3030df8c319d2d09c1e95\n\nEvaluated downstream Omni realtime change: https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang-omni/pull/2426\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38676014237](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38676014237)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38676014321](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38676014321)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38676014424](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38676014424)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n## Submission hygiene check (2026-10-15)\n\nAdded only the missing final newline to `test/manual/murmur_uint32/murmur_vector_results.json`, as reported by upstream CI. JSON values are unchanged; the preserved vector counts remain 72 original mismatches and 0 corrected mismatches. The sampling implementation is unchanged.\n\nCurrent submission head: `ebcec6e4a5416066688e6a5eb71af7476cf21ed7`. The earlier evaluated-source commit above remains the product-version reference. NPU PR tests on the previous head were blocked by the draft-PR gate and skipped, not a newly observed inference failure. This note does not claim the new upstream CI run is complete; keep this PR as a draft.\n",
