      "deletions": 0,
      "filename": "test/manual/murmur_uint32/README.md",
      "patch": "@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@\n+# Murmur32 high-bit regression\n+\n+Run `pytest test/manual/murmur_uint32/test_murmur_uint32_npu.py` in the patched SGLang release environment on an Ascend NPU. This is the existing 16-column regression. It uses deterministic integer reference values and skips without torch_npu / an NPU; a skip is not a hardware pass.\n+\n+`murmur_vector_results.json` is preserved evidence from a separate earlier 128-output check (8 seed/position pairs, 16 columns each). Original mismatches: 72; corrected mismatches: 0. All expected and observed integers are included. No fresh device run is claimed for packaging this evidence. No host identity, credentials, audio or model prompts are included.",
      "raw_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/raw/ebcec6e4a5416066688e6a5eb71af7476cf21ed7/test%2Fmanual%2Fmurmur_uint32%2FREADME.md",
      "sha": "f6aba89f76fe93dd9b1a837d5791c63e4c9f960f",
      "status": "added"
    },
